.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt LIBEXTENSIONCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libextensioncmp
.Nd system.SystemExtension client: kernel extension loads and policy queries through the BSDExtension provider
.Sh LIBRARY
.Pq libextensioncmp, Fl lextensioncmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In extensioncmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn service_ensure_extension "struct service_context *context" "const char *module"
.Ft int
.Fn service_extension_stat "struct service_context *context" "const char *module" "int *loadedp"
.Ft int
.Fn service_extension_list "struct service_context *context" "char (*names)[SERVICE_EXTENSION_NAME_MAX]" "size_t max" "size_t *countp"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_session_open "struct extensioncmp_session **sessionp"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_session_create "int fd" "struct extensioncmp_session **sessionp"
.Ft void
.Fn extensioncmp_session_close "struct extensioncmp_session *session"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_load "struct extensioncmp_session *session" "const char *module"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_stat "struct extensioncmp_session *session" "const char *module" "int *loadedp"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_list "struct extensioncmp_session *session" "char (*names)[SERVICE_EXTENSION_NAME_MAX]" "size_t max" "size_t *countp"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_reload "struct extensioncmp_session *session"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_manage "struct extensioncmp_session *session" "enum service_extension_action action" "const char *module"
.Ft int
.Fn extensioncmp_info "struct extensioncmp_session *session" "const char *name" "int next" "struct service_extension_info *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The context calls were part of
.Xr libservice 3
and moved to their own library with the same names and semantics.
Each takes the process's own service context from
.Xr service_acquire 3 ;
a context inherited across a fork is refused with
.Er EINVAL .
The calls speak the FIDL library
.Li bsd.extension.v1
.Pq Pa /usr/share/fidl/extensioncmp.fidl
to the provider.
The process-wide session is opened by name on first use and negotiated
once; a forked child abandons the parent's session and opens its own.
Each call is bounded by 30 seconds, shortened by an active
.Xr service_budget_begin 3 .
A timeout, a transport failure or a malformed reply drops the session, and
the next call opens a new one; an application error keeps it.
.Pp
.Fn service_ensure_extension
asks the
.Dq system.SystemExtension
provider
.Pq Xr BSDExtension 8
to ensure the kernel extension (module) named
.Fa module
is loaded (success includes an already-loaded module).
.Fa module
must be a single, safe filename component.
This is a
.Dv SYSTEM Ns -domain
caller only; the discovery domain layer makes the name unresolvable for user
services, so it fails closed for them.
.Pp
.Fn service_extension_stat
queries whether the kernel extension named
.Fa module
is loaded without attempting a load, setting
.Fa *loadedp
to 1 (loaded) or 0 (not).
It is routed and validated exactly like
.Fn service_ensure_extension ;
a denied name fails with
.Er EPERM .
.Pp
.Fn service_extension_list
enumerates the module names
.Xr BSDExtension 8 Ns 's
allow-list permits, so a consumer can discover what it may
.Fn service_ensure_extension
without probing names blindly.
It is routed exactly like the other extension calls: a
.Dv SYSTEM Ns -domain
caller only.
The allow-list is global rather than per-label, so every caller sees the same
set, and the reply reveals only which names may load, never any loaded or
not-loaded state.
Up to
.Fa max
names are written into
.Fa names ,
each a
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_NAME_MAX Ns -byte
NUL-terminated buffer, with their number stored in
.Fa countp .
The reply holds at most
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_LIST_MAX
entries; a larger effective policy fails with
.Er EOVERFLOW .
A smaller
.Fa max
that cannot hold it fails with
.Er EMSGSIZE ,
storing the required count in
.Fa *countp
rather than truncating silently.
.Pp
.Fn extensioncmp_load ,
.Fn extensioncmp_stat ,
and
.Fn extensioncmp_list
provide the same typed extension operations on a caller-owned
.Vt struct extensioncmp_session
instead of the process-wide one.
.Fn extensioncmp_session_open
opens the SystemExtension service by name;
.Fn extensioncmp_session_create
adopts a held channel descriptor, consuming it only on success;
.Fn extensioncmp_session_close
closes the session.
The typed calls neither acquire discovery authority nor close the session.
A transport failure, timeout or malformed reply ends the session: that call
fails
.Pq Er EPROTO No for a malformed reply
and every later call fails with the same error.
A session used in a forked child fails with
.Er ECHILD .
.Pp
.Fn extensioncmp_reload
takes a session and requests an atomic reload of the broker's configured
defaults file, preserving persistent administrator overrides.
It requires ADMIN rights on that service channel.
It accepts no path or policy contents; failures leave the active policy intact.
These functions return zero on success and minus one with errno on failure.
.Pp
.Fn extensioncmp_manage
requires ADMIN channel rights and accepts one of
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_ALLOW ,
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_DENY ,
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_RESET ,
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_ENABLE ,
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_DISABLE ,
or
.Dv SERVICE_EXTENSION_RESTORE .
ALLOW and DENY persist permission overrides; RESET removes the entire override,
including desired activation.
ENABLE records desired boot activation of an already permitted module;
DISABLE removes activation while retaining permission.
RESTORE takes no module name (pass NULL) and loads all permitted enabled
entries.
Permission and activation edits do not immediately load or forcibly unload code.
Persistent edits and restoration fail with
.Er EAGAIN
until administrator storage is attached, or
.Er EPERM
when authority or required permission is absent.
.Pp
.Fn extensioncmp_info
queries a named module with
.Fa next
set to zero, or returns the first known policy entry lexically after
.Fa name
with
.Fa next
set to one.
Start enumeration with an empty name, advance to each returned name, and stop on
.Er ENOENT .
The result contains
.Fa name , allowed , enabled , loaded , overridden ,
and
.Fa ready .
Loaded state is not disclosed for denied modules; ready indicates attached
administrator storage.
Each returned entry is coherent, but enumeration is not a snapshot across
concurrent policy edits.
This API avoids the list size limit.
See
.Xr sysextctl 8
for operator commands and persistence semantics.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std service_ensure_extension service_extension_stat service_extension_list extensioncmp_session_open extensioncmp_session_create extensioncmp_load extensioncmp_stat extensioncmp_list extensioncmp_reload extensioncmp_manage extensioncmp_info
.Sh ERRORS
In addition to the provider's
.Xr errno 2
values (for example
.Er EPERM , EAGAIN , ENOENT No or Er EOVERFLOW ):
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An argument was invalid, or
.Fa context
is not this process's own service context.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
The provider's reply was malformed; any descriptor it carried was closed.
.It Bq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
The provider speaks a different wire version.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
The provider did not answer in time.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr BSDExtension 8
.Sh HISTORY
The context functions appeared in
.Xr libservice 3 ;
.Nm libextensioncmp
appeared in 5BSD when they moved out of it, and its record protocol was
replaced by
.Li bsd.extension.v1
in October 2026, when the
.Fn extensioncmp_*
session calls replaced
.Fn service_session_extension_*
on a borrowed
.Vt struct service_session .
